<pre class="metadata">
title: TypedArray.prototype.search / searchLast / contains
stage: 1
contributors: James M Snell
</pre>

<emu-clause id="sec-typedarray-objects">
  <h1>TypedArray Objects</h1>

  <emu-clause id="sec-%typedarray%-intrinsic-object">
    <h1>The %TypedArray% Intrinsic Object</h1>

    <emu-clause id="sec-properties-of-the-%typedarrayprototype%-object">
      <h1>Properties of the %TypedArray% Prototype Object</h1>

      <emu-clause id="sec-%typedarray%.prototype.search">
        <h1>%TypedArray%.prototype.search ( _needle_ )</h1>
        <p>This method searches for the first occurrence of the subsequence _needle_ within this TypedArray. It performs the following steps when called:</p>
        <emu-alg>
          1. Let _O_ be the *this* value.
          1. Let _taRecord_ be ? ValidateTypedArray(_O_, ~seq-cst~).
          1. Let _needleRecord_ be ? ValidateTypedArray(_needle_, ~seq-cst~).
          1. If TypedArrayElementType(_O_) is not TypedArrayElementType(_needle_), throw a *TypeError* exception.
          1. Let _haystackLength_ be TypedArrayLength(_taRecord_).
          1. Let _needleLength_ be TypedArrayLength(_needleRecord_).
          1. If _needleLength_ is 0, return *+0*<sub>𝔽</sub>.
          1. If _needleLength_ &gt; _haystackLength_, return *-1*<sub>𝔽</sub>.
          1. Let _index_ be the smallest non-negative integer _k_ such that the subsequence of _O_ starting at _k_ with length _needleLength_ is SameValueZero-equal to _needle_, or *-1*<sub>𝔽</sub> if no such _k_ exists.
          1. Return _index_.
        </emu-alg>
        <emu-note>
          <p>This method requires that _needle_ be a TypedArray of the same type as the *this* value. For example, if *this* is a `Uint8Array`, then _needle_ must also be a `Uint8Array`.</p>
          <p>Two subsequences are <dfn>SameValueZero-equal</dfn> if they have the same length and for each index, the corresponding elements are equal according to the SameValueZero algorithm. This means that for floating-point TypedArrays (Float32Array, Float64Array, Float16Array), *NaN* values are considered equal to each other regardless of their bit patterns, and *+0*<sub>𝔽</sub> is considered equal to *-0*<sub>𝔽</sub>.</p>
          <p>Implementations may use any technique to search for the subsequence, such as naive search, Boyer-Moore, or other string matching algorithms, provided the observable result is the index of the first occurrence of the subsequence or *-1*<sub>𝔽</sub> if not found.</p>
        </emu-note>
      </emu-clause>

      <emu-clause id="sec-%typedarray%.prototype.searchlast">
        <h1>%TypedArray%.prototype.searchLast ( _needle_ )</h1>
        <p>This method searches for the last occurrence of the subsequence _needle_ within this TypedArray. It performs the following steps when called:</p>
        <emu-alg>
          1. Let _O_ be the *this* value.
          1. Let _taRecord_ be ? ValidateTypedArray(_O_, ~seq-cst~).
          1. Let _needleRecord_ be ? ValidateTypedArray(_needle_, ~seq-cst~).
          1. If TypedArrayElementType(_O_) is not TypedArrayElementType(_needle_), throw a *TypeError* exception.
          1. Let _haystackLength_ be TypedArrayLength(_taRecord_).
          1. Let _needleLength_ be TypedArrayLength(_needleRecord_).
          1. If _needleLength_ is 0, return 𝔽(_haystackLength_).
          1. If _needleLength_ &gt; _haystackLength_, return *-1*<sub>𝔽</sub>.
          1. Let _index_ be the largest non-negative integer _k_ such that _k_ + _needleLength_ ≤ _haystackLength_ and the subsequence of _O_ starting at _k_ with length _needleLength_ is SameValueZero-equal to _needle_, or *-1*<sub>𝔽</sub> if no such _k_ exists.
          1. Return _index_.
        </emu-alg>
        <emu-note>
          <p>This method requires that _needle_ be a TypedArray of the same type as the *this* value. For example, if *this* is a `Uint8Array`, then _needle_ must also be a `Uint8Array`.</p>
          <p>Two subsequences are SameValueZero-equal if they have the same length and for each index, the corresponding elements are equal according to the SameValueZero algorithm. This means that for floating-point TypedArrays (Float32Array, Float64Array, Float16Array), *NaN* values are considered equal to each other regardless of their bit patterns, and *+0*<sub>𝔽</sub> is considered equal to *-0*<sub>𝔽</sub>.</p>
          <p>Implementations may use any technique to search for the subsequence, such as naive search, Boyer-Moore, or other string matching algorithms, provided the observable result is the index of the last occurrence of the subsequence or *-1*<sub>𝔽</sub> if not found.</p>
        </emu-note>
      </emu-clause>

      <emu-clause id="sec-%typedarray%.prototype.contains">
        <h1>%TypedArray%.prototype.contains ( _needle_ )</h1>
        <p>This method determines whether the subsequence _needle_ exists within this TypedArray. It performs the following steps when called:</p>
        <emu-alg>
          1. Let _O_ be the *this* value.
          1. Let _taRecord_ be ? ValidateTypedArray(_O_, ~seq-cst~).
          1. Let _needleRecord_ be ? ValidateTypedArray(_needle_, ~seq-cst~).
          1. If TypedArrayElementType(_O_) is not TypedArrayElementType(_needle_), throw a *TypeError* exception.
          1. Let _haystackLength_ be TypedArrayLength(_taRecord_).
          1. Let _needleLength_ be TypedArrayLength(_needleRecord_).
          1. If _needleLength_ is 0, return *true*.
          1. If _needleLength_ &gt; _haystackLength_, return *false*.
          1. Return *true* if there exists a non-negative integer _k_ such that _k_ + _needleLength_ ≤ _haystackLength_ and the subsequence of _O_ starting at _k_ with length _needleLength_ is SameValueZero-equal to _needle_; otherwise return *false*.
        </emu-alg>
        <emu-note>
          <p>This method requires that _needle_ be a TypedArray of the same type as the *this* value. For example, if *this* is a `Uint8Array`, then _needle_ must also be a `Uint8Array`.</p>
          <p>Two subsequences are SameValueZero-equal if they have the same length and for each index, the corresponding elements are equal according to the SameValueZero algorithm. This means that for floating-point TypedArrays (Float32Array, Float64Array, Float16Array), *NaN* values are considered equal to each other regardless of their bit patterns, and *+0*<sub>𝔽</sub> is considered equal to *-0*<sub>𝔽</sub>.</p>
          <p>Implementations may use any technique to search for the subsequence, such as naive search, Boyer-Moore, or other string matching algorithms, provided the observable result correctly indicates whether the subsequence exists.</p>
        </emu-note>
      </emu-clause>
    </emu-clause>
  </emu-clause>
</emu-clause>
